# Design Controls

<!-- merged from: atlas/06-atlas-design-controls -->

> **Source of truth = Atlas Design Controls MCP** (`user-atlas-design-controls`). See `mcp-sole-source.mdc`. All reads and writes go through the MCP.

Traceability chain: `UN → DI → DO (code) → VT → VAL`.

## Document ID Patterns

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| User Need | `UN-ATLAS-XXX` | `UN-ATLAS-001` |
| Design Input | `DI-ATLAS-XXX` | `DI-ATLAS-042` |
| Design Output | `DO-ATLAS-XXX-YYY` | `DO-ATLAS-042-001` |
| Risk | `R-ATLAS-XXX` | `R-ATLAS-007` |
| Hazard | `H-ATLAS-XXX` | `H-ATLAS-003` |
| Verification Test | `VT-ATLAS-XXX` | `VT-ATLAS-003` |
| Validation Test | `VAL-ATLAS-XXX` | `VAL-ATLAS-001` |

- IDs are stable — never silently delete or renumber.
- Never reuse a retired ID; mark obsolete IDs as `[OBSOLETE]`.
- All DI requirements use "The system shall…" wording.

## Change Classification

| Class | Description | Action required |
|---|---|---|
| Cosmetic | Whitespace, comments, docs | None |
| A | Internal refactor, no behaviour change | Update DO |
| B | New or changed behaviour, non-safety-critical | Update DI + DO + VT |
| C | Safety-critical change | Full DI → DO → Risk → VT → VAL cycle + CSO review |

## Required on New Work

- Read design controls **before** making any Class B/C change.
- Add DI / DO / VT references in file headers.
- Add file headers for Safety Class B/C:
  ```
  # UN: UN-ATLAS-XXX | DI: DI-ATLAS-XXX | DO: DO-ATLAS-XXX | Safety Class: B
  ```
- Update DO status to `implemented` then `verified` via `update_design_output`.
- Read the current traceability matrix with `get_traceability_matrix`; check gaps with `get_traceability_gaps`.

## Audit Codebase Before Acting

1. Search the codebase to understand existing patterns and reuse them.
2. Minimise the change surface — touch only what is necessary.
3. Duplicate code is a failure; extract and reuse.
